    "collapsible_content_aqyrc4": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_jP3dUU": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What does a typical training day look like?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The morning session will predominately focus on the theory required to test and tag, while the afternoon focuses heavily on learning to test and tag with a portable appliance tester. All of our classes in WA are kept to a maximum of 12 people so that everyone in the room can get individual time and support from our trainer. Upon completing the course, you should be completely comfortable at testing and tagging on your own. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_wgai4y": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Where are your locations in WA?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We have 4 different locations for you to choose from - Perth, Fremantle, Cockburn and Como. Alternatively, you can reach out to our friendly team on <a href=\"tel:1300848302\" title=\"tel:1300848302\">1300 848 302</a> and they'll be more than happy to book a spot for you. We also provide onsite training across WA if you have a group of people requiring training. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_YAFc4k": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does the Course go for?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Our 1 day comprehensive course generally starts at 8:00 am and finishes at approximately 4:30 pm, with breaks for morning tea and lunch. If you’re planning on doing the Nationally Recognised course, it’ll consist of an additional self-paced WHS online component, which is to be completed in your own time before the course date. This typically takes around 3-4 hours, depending on your existing knowledge. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_DhYd67": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Who will be the instructor on the day? ",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Our WA trainer is Russ Tuff, a previous test and tag owner for the past 5 years and an electrician with over 18 years of experience. More than just conveying knowledge, Russ<br/>ignites a passion for electrical safety in his students. His engaging and<br/>personalised approach ensures all learners, regardless of prior experience,<br/>feel confident and equipped to succeed in the electrical testing and tagging<br/>field. Russ consistently receives 5 star reviews for his courses and we guarantee you won't be disappointed. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_XjqzKP": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What if I need technical support after the course? ",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>You’ll have the peace of mind knowing that we'll be there when you need us, whether it's by phone, email or in person. Every single student taught by Test & Tag Training receives free lifetime technical support from our team of experts. Guaranteed. This could be anything from how to use a specific appliance tester or how to test and tag a particular electrical appliance. We want to ensure we're making people's jobs easier by offering dependable service and expert advice when you need it most.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_pDpFbG": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do I need to bring anything for the training day?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>To ensure a comprehensive learning experience, it's mandatory to have access to a <a href=\"/pages/portable-appliance-testers\" title=\"Portable Appliance Testers\">PAT Tester</a> for the hands-on training section. If you don't already have one, you can buy or borrow a PAT Tester from us via Appliance Testing Supplies. This way, you’ll get hands-on experience using the actual appliance tester you use in the real world. Our Perth head office stocks a complete range of PAT Testers before your course.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
